course: dictionary
lesson: 13453
title: Short forms: hr and HR
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short way of writing a word. «hr» is short for «hour», and «hrs» is short for «hours». You will see them in maths, on timetables and on signs. «The film lasts 2 hrs 30 min.» That means two hours and thirty minutes.
explain: Capital letters change the meaning. «HR» in capitals is not about time. It stands for «human resources», the part of a company that looks after hiring and workers. «My aunt works in HR at a big company.»
explain: Speed can use «hr» too. «The train travels at 100 km/hr.» Many people now write «km/h» instead, which is the better form. When you read «hr» aloud, say "hour", and the sentence will make sense.
fact: «hr» is short for «hour», and «hrs» is short for «hours».
fact: «HR» in capitals stands for «human resources», the part of a company that looks after hiring and workers.
fact: «24 hr shop» means a shop that is open for 24 hours.
fact: When you see «hr» in a sum or on a timetable, read it aloud as "hour" to check your meaning.
exercise: «The bus ride takes 2 hrs.» What does «hrs» stand for? | minutes | heroes | *hours
exercise: Sam sees a sign: «Open 24 hr.» What does it mean? | The shop sells 24 hats | *The shop is open all day and all night | The shop is open for 24 minutes | The shop is closed for 24 days
exercise: Mum says, «I work in HR.» What does HR stand for? | Hot railway | *Human resources | Hours and minutes | Home reading
test: «The match lasted 1 hr 45 min.» How many hours was the match? | *1 | 100 | 45 | 2
test: «The car drove at 80 km/hr.» What does hr mean here? | *hour | hall | hair | minute
exam: Which short form means more than one hour? | hh | HR | hr | *hrs
